sched: enable HRTICK by default on l4h

The l4h guest has a high-resolution clockevent, so CFS slices shorter
than the tick are honoured with the hrtick.  The default is chosen with
#ifdef, not IS_ENABLED(): with CONFIG_JUMP_LABEL, sched.h and debug.c
paste the default into static_key_##enabled and jump_label_key__##enabled,
so it must be the literal true or false.

--- a/kernel/sched/features.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/features.h
@@ -63,7 +63,12 @@ SCHED_FEAT(DELAY_ZERO, true)
  */
 SCHED_FEAT(WAKEUP_PREEMPTION, true)
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_L4H
+/* L4H has a high-resolution clockevent; honor CFS slices below the tick. */
+SCHED_FEAT(HRTICK, true)
+#else
 SCHED_FEAT(HRTICK, false)
+#endif
 SCHED_FEAT(HRTICK_DL, false)
 
